MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_001: I understand that my mother, Yu Phas, hid her face\nbehind a mask while living in the temple of Balor.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_002: There was a prophecy from the progenitor god that\nbad luck would follow if her face went uncovered.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_003: But, when my father inadvertently saw her face\nduring his visit to the Isle of Sorrows...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_004: Well, he fell in love with her and implored her to\nleave the island with him.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_005: The story goes that she resisted my father's advances\nat first.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_006: In truth, she was never altogether displeased with\nthe idea. They were a wonderful couple.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_007: Still, she did always seem to be a little melancholy.\nIt's hard to explain.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01_008: At the time, I didn't understand how she could\nfeel that way. 
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Aur_m01: <BLN>There was a prophecy...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_001: I was thinking about the Zenzele situation. And now\nI have a slight suspicion about Lord Solel.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_002: Is it possible he had that barrier installed to ensure\nyour mom's safety?
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_003: I wonder if maybe he was trying to keep people out,\nrather than keep her in.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_004: That barrier would also serve as proof that she was\nlocked inside when more people vanished, right?
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_005: <NCA>Say she's overthinking it.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_006: <NCB>Agree it's possible.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_007: <ACA>At the very least, you have to admit there's no need\nfor a barrier so extreme—to lock away one woman.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_008: If protecting her was Lord Solel's true intention...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01_009: I suppose I could revise my opinion of him. A little.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Tia_m01: <BLN>I think I've figured something out...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m01_001: Well. It's finally time, huh? To be honest, it got here\na little quicker than I'd hoped.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m01_002: We have to fight the scary queen.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m01_003: I'm scared, but I'm going to fight the best I can.\nYou just watch me!
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m01_004: This is my chance to prove myself to Tialla.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Pet_m01: <BLN>It's finally time...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m02_001: I can't stop worrying about who we'll face next in the\nHeroic Games.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m02_002: Maybe that's why I used to be able to eat four bowls\nof rice...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m02_003: but these days, I'm full after barely three.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Pet_m02_004: If this keeps up, I might waste away...
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Pet_m02: <BLN>I can't stop worrying...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01_001: I still get chills when I think about being inside\nthat painting.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01_002: Zenzele called all of us his family.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01_003: But that's no way to treat family.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01_004: I felt more like a doll, sitting on Zenzele's shelf. I was\njust there to be looked at.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01_005: I'm so glad I made it back to this side of the canvas.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01_006: I have to say, a regular old life, with nothing much\ngoing on? Might be the happiest you can be.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01_007: Cai, I'll never forget what you did for me...what I\nowe you, for the rest of my life!
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Hur_m01: <BLN>I'll never forget...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01_001: Gabriel says your next match is against the queen\nof Saramis?
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01_002: I've heard the rumors, and I don't imagine that lady\ndoes things by halves.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01_003: You know they call her the "Iron Bastion" back\nin Saramis.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01_004: And her entire crew is a bunch of legitimately\ntough guys who've fought on real battlefields.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01_005: Saramis is always getting involved in one war or\nanother with their neighbors, the Mosa.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01_006: Be careful out there, OK? Don't want to get hurt\nbefore your match even starts.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Cas_m01: <BLN>Keep it together!
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m02_001: You seem...different, lately.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m02_002: I don't know quite how to put it except that you're\nstarting to look more like a man than a kid.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m02_003: Don't let it go to your head, alright?
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cas_m02_004: Easiest way to lose a fight is to be overly sure that\nyou're going to win it.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Cas_m02: <BLN>Don't let it go to your head.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_001: Castor and I are opposites in many ways, but we've\nstill been friends since the earliest times.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_002: I got to know him when he was still a candidate for\nthe vulkans.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_003: Believe it or not, I was his instructor.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_004: He was incredibly skilled at a young age, but his\nbehavior was problematic in the extreme.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_005: That's how he came by the name Windstorm.\nIt wasn't given to him as a compliment.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_006: Estie and I, both his seniors, had to clean up an\nawful lot of his messes.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_007: Because of that history, Castor has never been able\nto stand as an equal with Estie.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_008: Hmm? Estie? You know her very well, Cai.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01_009: Peter's mother. Yes, that Estie.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c10_Cen_m01: <BLN>Want to hear a story?